WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.570
&gt;&gt;&gt; WYOMING HAS THE SMALLEST
POPULATION IN THE COUNTRY, YET

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.405
ITS CONGRESSIONAL PRIMARY RACE
TOMORROW IS HIGHLY ANTICIPATED.

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.509
THE COWBOY STATE HAS ONLY ONE
CONGRESSIONAL SEAT, AND RIGHT

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.679
NOW IT'S FILLED BY REPUBLICAN
LIZ CHENEY.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.649
BUT IT IS AN UPHILL BATTLE FOR
HER TO KEEP THAT SEAT AFTER SHE

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.352
VOTED TO IMPEACH DONALD TRUMP
AND THEN BECAME THE VICE CHAIR

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.755
OF THE JANUARY 6th COMMITTEE.
TRUMP WON WYOMING WITH ALMOST

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:27.994
70% OF THE VOTE IN 2020.
AND AT THE MOMENT, CHENEY IS

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:33.766
RUNNING ALMOST 30 PERCENTAGE
POINTS BEHIND HER TRUMP-BACKED

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:38.137
OPPONENT HARRIET HAGEMAN.
CHENEY IS EVEN ASKING DEMOCRATS

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:39.639
TO SWITCH PARTIES TO VOTE FOR
HER.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:43.943
I WANT TO GET PERSPECTIVE FROM
TWO WYOMING VOTERS, ONE WHO DID

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.580
SWITCH PARTIES JUST TO VOTE FOR
CHENEY, AND THE OTHER A

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.351
REPUBLICAN WHO PLANS TO VOTE
AGAINST LIZ CHENEY.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.620
LET'S START WITH MYRNA.
THANKS SO MUCH FOR YOUR TIME.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.356
WHAT DON'T YOU LIKE ABOUT LIZ
CHENEY?

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.592
&gt;&gt; WELL, I THINK ONE THING THAT
STANDS OUT TO ME AT THIS POINT

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:05.131
IN TIME IS THAT, WHILE SHE HAS
BEEN A VERY CONSERVATIVE VOTE IN

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:10.403
THE LEGISLATURE, SHE JUST SEEMS
TO BE SWINGING A LITTLE BIT MORE

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:14.607
TOWARD THE LEFT.
BUT EVEN BEFORE THAT IN THE LAST

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:19.145
COUPLE OF YEARS, IT JUST DOES
NOT FEEL SHE REALLY REPRESENTS

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.748
THE STATE ANYMORE.
&gt;&gt; LET'S TALK ABOUT THAT, MYRNA,

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.551
BECAUSE WHEN YOU SAY SHE'S
SWINGING MORE TOWARDS THE LEFT,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:27.654
I THINK SHE VOTED ON -- IN TERMS
OF THE ISSUES, SHE IS WHERE

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.256
DONALD TRUMP IS.
SHE VOTED WITH DONALD TRUMP I

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:34.727
THINK ON 93% OF THE TIME.
SHE'S CONSERVATIVE.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.929
AND SO --
&gt;&gt; I GET THAT.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.898
&gt;&gt; YEAH.
SO, WHAT -- IN TERMS OF -- WHY

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.401
AREN'T THOSE ISSUES OR HER
POSITIONS ON THOSE ISSUES AS

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:46.739
IMPORTANT TO YOU?
&gt;&gt; WELL, LIKE I SAY, THAT HAS

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.876
BEEN THE CASE.
BUT HERE RECENTLY -- I MEAN, YOU

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:57.016
TAKE, FOR EXAMPLE, THE GUN VOTE.
THAT IS NOT PRO-WYOMING.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.252
SHE IS NOT REPRESENTING HER
CONSTITUENTS ANYMORE.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:05.325
WHEN YOU START VOTING AGAINST
GUN S AND THE SECOND AMENDMENT,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:09.295
THAT BECOMES AN ISSUE FOR A
LARGE NUMBER OF WYOMINGENS.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:15.501
AND YOU LOOK AT THE CHIP BILL.
THAT'S A CORPORATE GIVE AWAY.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.937
AND THAT'S NOT EXACTLY A
CONSERVATIVE VOTE AS WELL.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.474
&gt;&gt; HOW DO YOU FEEL ABOUT THE
ROLE HE'S PLAYED IN

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.911
INVESTIGATING THE JANUARY 6th
INVESTIGATION?

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.247
&gt;&gt; I DON'T LIKE IT.
&gt;&gt; WHY NOT?

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:30.883
&gt;&gt; I FEEL LIKE -- WELL, I FEEL
LIKE SHE DID NOT EVEN BOTHER TO

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.753
STOP AT THE VERY INCEPTION OF
THIS.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.290
